CloudBurrow patch 9 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1126).

The bug: a negative INTERVAL of less than an hour, INTERVAL -1 SECOND or
MAKE_INTERVAL(second => -1), was written 0-0 0 0:0:1: IntervalValue.String
wrote the sign of the H:M:S part only through the hours field. The engine
stores and passes an interval as that text, so the value read back (and
compared, and returned) was positive; ParseInterval, likewise, read the sign
of -0:0:1 and -0-1 from a field that is 0. And INTERVAL n MILLISECOND and
INTERVAL n MICROSECOND failed "unexpected interval part", although
BigQuery's INTERVAL takes both. The patch writes and reads each part's sign
as BigQuery's canonical format has it ([sign]Y-M [sign]D [sign]H:M:S[.F]),
and takes the two parts. interval_sign_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it.

